        "abstract": "THE RECENT environmental global goals have brought a significant inclination of industries toward renewable and clean energy. One of the major aims of the proliferation of renewable energy sources is achieving net-zero, that is, building a community where at least as much energy is produced as it is consumed with zero or negligible emissions [1]. The role of 6G communications is crucial for achieving net-zero. For example, reliable and seamless communications among energy sources, suppliers, and consumers can make the smart grid more responsive, adjusting dynamically to demand fluctuations and reducing energy wastage [2].",
